eering, artificial intelligence and machine learning, and data visualization.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(KCM-HE, SBA-HE)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: Executive Master of Public Administration students.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": ["Students will embed a data-driven strategic approach into their organization or product.", "Students will demonstrate understanding of the types of data in different types of organizations and products, the challenges faced with data quality, leadership, and team building.", "Students will anticipate use cases for artificial intelligence, machine learning, and data engineering pertinent to their organization or policy.", "Students will articulate the key ethical concerns with data security, data privacy, and artificial intelligence implementation and usage."], "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "HE", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2818, "crseId": 371569, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "PADM", "catalogNbr": "5113", "titleShort": "Public Administration & SP", "titleLong": "Public Administration: A Strategic Planning Perspective", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 1626, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "08:00PM", "timeEnd": "09:30PM", "startDt": "05/31/2022", "endDt": "07/02/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "tjo22", "firstName": "Thomas", "middleName": "J.", "lastName": "O'Toole"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "